<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Adaptive-icon foreground layer, injected into the built APK by
  scripts/patch_android_icon.sh (dioxus-cli 0.7.9 hardcodes its own default
  icon and offers no config hook - see that script's header).

  Deliberately a self-contained vector with no <bitmap android:src=...>
  reference: the foreground CANNOT point at @mipmap/ic_launcher, because on
  API 26+ that name resolves to mipmap-anydpi-v26/ic_launcher.xml - this
  adaptive icon itself - so the icon would reference itself, fail to
  inflate, and the launcher would silently fall back to its generic default
  app icon.

  Geometry: 108x108dp canvas, but only the central 72dp circle is
  guaranteed visible under every launcher mask. The artwork is an X of two
  swords, so its extreme points are its bounding-box corners; the box is
  sized 50dp so those corners sit at radius ~34.9, just inside the 36 limit.

  Path data is the U+2694 CROSSED SWORDS glyph outline from Noto Emoji
  (Apache-2.0), extracted with fontTools and transformed into the viewport
  above. Same artwork as assets/icon-512.png (the legacy pre-API-26 bitmap
  source); keep the two in sync if the icon ever changes.
-->
